    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first two battles of the Mexican‑American War, Palo Alto and Resaca de la Palma, were fought inside Brownsville’s borders.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26,
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://brownsvillehistory.org/discover-brownsville-history-brownsville-historical-association.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Brownsville’s Heritage Museum, Stillman House Museum, and Costumes of the Americas Museum preserve the town’s rich cultural history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://brownsvillehistory.org/discover-brownsville-history-brownsville-historical-association.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Brownsville sits between the Mexican border and South Padre Island, enjoying a semi‑tropical climate most of the year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://brownsvillehistory.org/discover-brownsville-history-brownsville-historical-association.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Mexican‑American War sparked a steamboat boom on the Rio Grande, making Brownsville a key river port.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://brownsvillehistory.org/discover-brownsville-history-brownsville-historical-association.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Before European settlement, nomadic Coahuiltecans, Lipan Apaches, and Karankawas roamed the area that is now Brownsville.",
